<!--
    Vocabulary extraction pass over BS EN 50742-2025 ("Approach B product requirements",
    clause 7 - the machinery Safety-Related Security Level (SRSL) requirements), part of the
    normative-coverage completion pass. Chosen over the other 8 remaining undocumented norms
    after a real triage (see design-session/SESSION.md): unlike IEC 62443-3-3's baseline SR/RE
    (verified via its own clause 4.1 to be control-SYSTEM-level, not component-level - a
    DeviceGroup/zone concern, not ProductFeature) and unlike most of the other 8 (organizational
    process/legal-definitional/methodology content), this document's clause 7 is explicitly
    titled "Product requirements" and clause 4.2 confirms machine/product-level scope
    ("the design and the construction of machinery shall not allow hazardous situations via
    connections").

    All 15 records below cite their real X.Y.Z "shall" clause (read in full from
    tools/norm-indexer/work/ir/clauses.jsonl, not the graph API's 4000-char truncation).
    SRSL tiering: 7.4.3.x clauses grade their requirement across SRSL0 (none)/SRSL1/SRSL2/SRSL3
    (stricter each level) - captured at the SRSL1 (first non-trivial) tier as the baseline
    testable requirement, same "base level, not every enhancement" scope discipline already
    used for IEC 62443-4-2's SR/CR base requirements vs REs. FEAT_BSEN50742_SW_AUTHENTICITY is
    the one exception: its SRSL1 tier is "None", so SRSL2 (the first non-trivial tier) is cited
    instead - verified directly in the source text, not assumed to follow the SRSL1 default.

    productFeatureTypeEnumId=PftSecurityCapability throughout (not PftSafetyFunction): these are
    security controls in service of safety (the norm's own term is "Safety-related Security
    level"), matching the existing distinction already established for ISO/TR 22100-4's 5
    security-control features vs ISO 12100's PftSafetyFunction behavioral requirements.

    Grouping follows the document's own real clause structure (7.2 Security measures / 7.3
    Information collection / 7.4 Protection measures against corruption) - not an arbitrary
    split. New ProductCategory NCAT_BSEN50742_SAFETY_SECURITY: this document's scope (any
    machine with safety functions and digital interfaces) does not match any existing IEC
    62443-4-2 component-type category (those are IACS-component-scoped: Software Application/
    Embedded/Host/Network Device), so reusing one would misrepresent the applicability - a new
    category is the honest choice here, unlike EN 40000-1-3 where reuse was the honest choice.
-->
